# Security Rules — Non-Negotiable

## Input

- SQL: Query Builder / `escape()` only — never concatenate user input
- XSS: `htmlspecialchars($v, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')` in views — no raw `<?= $var ?>`
- Use `$this->input->post()` / `$this->input->get()` — no raw `$_GET`/`$_POST`
- CSRF on every POST form and AJAX request
- Do NOT add `csrf_exclude_uris` without explicit approval

## Auth

- `require_module_access()` at top of protected controller methods
- `has_module_access()` in views for conditional UI
- Admin `role_id = 1` bypasses route RBAC
- Session: regenerate ID after login, full `sess_destroy()` on logout
- Never store passwords, tokens, or API keys in session

## Secrets

Store in `settings` / `api_integrations` table or env config — never hardcode. Never commit `database.php`, `email.php`, or API keys.

## File Uploads

- CI upload lib, auto-generated filenames (block `../`)
- Validate MIME via `finfo_file()`, scan for `<?php` tags in content
- Allowed: jpg/jpeg/png/webp/pdf/xlsx/csv, max 5MB, path `uploads/{module}/`
- Downloads: proxy via controller + auth check + `Content-Disposition: attachment`

## Errors

Never expose DB credentials, stack traces, or raw errors to frontend. Return generic HTTP 500 message. `log_message('error', ...)` with full context server-side.

## Sensitive Endpoints (auth/payments/PHI)

- Rate limit login/OTP: max 5 attempts, 15 min lockout, generic 429
- Idempotency keys on payment/booking inserts
- Webhooks: validate HMAC with `hash_equals()`, log payload first, return 200 within 5s
- Never log passwords, raw JWT, or full PII — mask emails/phones

## HTTPS & Headers

HTTPS enforced via `.htaccess`. Set `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, CSP.
